DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout Chris D’Elia\nChris D’El
	ia is one of the most in-demand stand-up comedians working today. Known fo
	r his high-energy performances\, razor-sharp wit\, and fearless crowd work
	\, D’Elia has built a massive following through his Netflix specials — inc
	luding Man on Fire (2017)\, Incorrigible (2015)\, and his appearance in Ne
	tflix’s Comedians of the World series. His debut special White Male\, Blac
	k Comic premiered on Comedy Central in 2013. Beyond stand-up\, D’Elia is a
	 beloved podcast host — his show Congratulations with Chris D’Elia has bee
	n a top comedy podcast on iTunes since 2017. He’s also a co-star on The Go
	lden Hour with Brendan Schaub. \nWhat to Expect\nA Chris D’Elia show is an
	 experience unlike any other. Expect rapid-fire delivery\, hilarious perso
	nal stories\, and spontaneous crowd interaction that keeps the entire room
	 on edge. D’Elia’s comedy blends self-deprecating humor with bold observat
	ions about relationships\, pop culture\, and everyday life. His energy is 
	electric — he rarely stays still on stage — and his ability to improvise a
	nd riff with the audience makes every show feel completely unique. This is
	 a 21+ event\, so expect a mature\, no-holds-barred performance. \nAbout B
	rea Improv\nThe Brea Improv is one of Southern California’s premier comedy
	 clubs\, located at 180 S Brea Blvd in Brea\, CA — just 30 miles southeast
	 of downtown Los Angeles. Part of the nationally renowned Improv Comedy Cl
	ub chain\, the Brea location features an intimate showroom with general ad
	mission seating\, premium booths\, and a full food and beverage menu. The 
	club has a mandatory two-item minimum per guest in the showroom\, making i
	t a true dinner-and-a-show experience. With its cozy atmosphere and excell
	ent sightlines\, every seat feels close to the stage. \nEvent Details\n\nD
	ate: Friday\, July 10\, 2026\nTime: 7:30 PM PDT (Doors open at 6:00 PM)\nV
	enue: Brea Improv\, 180 S Brea Blvd\, Brea\, CA 92821\nAge Requirement: 21
	+\nTicket Prices: $35 – $100 (plus fees)\n\nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets
	 \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extr
